## Performance and Synchronization

One of the most frequently repeated claims in Zakura’s official materials is its synchronization speed. In the release announcement, blockchain synchronization over the standard P2P network is said to complete in about **4 hours 20 minutes**, compared with **20 hours 46 minutes** for Zebra in their published test results. 

Furthermore, when using snapshots, bootstrap time can be reduced dramatically. In the official illustration, an *archive snapshot* can cut the time down to around **37 minutes 9 seconds**, while a *pruned snapshot* can make the node ready in only about **1 minute 50 seconds**. 

It is worth noting that these figures were published by the project team and reflect their testing conditions. Still, the overall message is clear: **Zakura treats fast synchronization as a major differentiator**. 

